hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1371","Musa bin Abdul Rahman Al Masruqi told us, Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Burayd, meaning Ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, He said: The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he got up in fear, fearing that the Hour would come, so he got up until he came to the mosque, then he got up. He prays with the longest standing, bowing, and prostration that I have ever seen him do in a prayer. Then he said: “These signs that God sends are not for the death of anyone.” Nor for his life, but God sends it to frighten His servants with it, so if you see any of it, be terrified to mention it and supplicate to it. And ask for His forgiveness.”"
